<h1><%= @playthrough.story.title %></h1>
<%# The window into the machine, and the only mark it leaves on the game.
    Absent entirely unless `Playthrough::Debug.enabled?` -- local by default --
    so a player who was handed a playthrough link is never shown one. %>
<p>
  <%= link_to "&larr; all stories".html_safe, root_path %>
  <% if Playthrough::Debug.enabled? %>
    &middot; <%= link_to "debug", playthrough_debug_path(@playthrough) %>
  <% end %>
</p>

<div class="preface"><%= @playthrough.story.preface %></div>
<hr>

<%# THE CABLE. Everything a turn changes is broadcast onto this playthrough's
    stream by NarrationJob: batched chunks of prose while it narrates, then the
    finished `#turn_log` when it lands. Outside `#turn_log` on purpose -- a
    subscription element inside the element being replaced would be torn down
    and rebuilt on every turn, and the tail of the turn would go to a channel
    nobody was listening on yet. %>
<%= turbo_stream_from @playthrough %>

<%= render "playthroughs/turn_log", playthrough: @playthrough, command: nil %>

<%# Where the player left off. A plain reload and the index's Resume link both
    aim at `#bottom`, so the browser puts the newest turn on screen with no
    script involved. A brand new playthrough is the deliberate exception:
    PlaythroughsController#create sends the player to the top, where the preface
    and the opening arrival are.

    Taking a turn no longer arrives here at all -- there is no redirect left to
    carry an anchor -- so where the viewport sits while prose arrives is
    `app/javascript/play.js`'s job, and it follows the narration down only while
    the player is already reading the bottom. %>
<div id="bottom"></div>
